    {
     "type": "note",
     "title": "Word order in W-questions",
     "md": "**W-word → verb → subject → rest**\n\n- {de:Wo wohnst du?}\n- {de:Warum lernst du Deutsch?}\n- {de:Wann kommt der Zug?}\n\n**wo / woher / wohin**: *wo* = where (a place), *woher* = where from, *wohin* = where to. English often just says *where*, German doesn't.\n\n**wie viel / wie viele**: *wie viel* + things you can't count (*Wasser, Geld*), *wie viele* + plural (*Zähne, Stunden*)."
